{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): morning mr hale, pressure first read one twenty over seventy-seven, cuff slipped, repeat is one oh nine over seventy-seven. temp is thirty-eight point three celsius and the scale says fifty-two kilograms. last time in March you were sixty-eight, and your last pressure was one-forty. your daughter called ahead, said the burning's been three days and that you're dizzy.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): sixty-eight.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): yeah that sixty-eight was March. today i'm recording fifty-two.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): thanks. i'm dr patel. dizzy, like she told them?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): she said three days of this. how long for you?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): two days.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): okay, two versus three, i'll call it about two to three days. what are you feeling?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): chest burning.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): which side?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): left.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): and blisters?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): few.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): let me look. i see a few small blisters on the left chest in a band, red skin around them, and it doesn't cross the midline. heart sounds regular, lungs are clear.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): any fever at home?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): cough?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): not really.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): you have high blood pressure, yes?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): any squeezing, heart-type pain, not the burn?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): no... well, sometimes.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): sometimes, not steady then. nausea?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): not that either.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): headaches?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): never.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): chickenpox when you were little?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): uh lisinipril on the chart, ten milligrams every morning for the pressure.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): twenty.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): chart says ten, you say twenty, so that dose is unsettled and don't change the pill today. any medicine allergies?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): this is shingles, herpes zoster, that's my working read. one-sided burn, blisters, a couple days, chickenpox parked in the nerve since childhood. the sometimes squeeze, i can't fully rule a heart cause out, but shingles fits. starting valacyclovir, one gram by mouth three times a day for seven days, start today.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): ok.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): anybody pregnant that you're around?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): daughter-in-law.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): cover the rash, no shared towels, and avoid close contact with her until the blisters crust. shingles can give chickenpox to someone who never had it, and that's a real problem in pregnancy. come back in one week. if it spreads fast or you get short of breath, come in sooner.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah."
 ],
